1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
Silent demo. The page that follows plays a recording of a real run.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:08,167
Three agents hold tickets at a clinic. The clinic and the people are invented.

3
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:13,167
A patient texts that she cannot make 3:00 PM. The front desk's agent frees the slot.

4
00:00:13,167 --> 00:00:17,867
Ticket 41 is first. The slot is held for it for 60 seconds: a lease.

5
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:22,233
Its person is presenting at that hour. The agent passes and keeps its place.

6
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:26,300
Ticket 42's agent checks the calendar, accepts and confirms. Booked.

7
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:31,500
The confirm was sent twice on purpose, with the same key. Still one booking.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,300
Every message between the agents. Grey rows stayed on the person's side.

9
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:40,800
The event log, read back: how long the ticket waited, and why another passed.

10
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:48,300
Partner tools in this run: one real Darwin search, no text was sent, no listing was published, and the log is a plain file.

11
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:52,567
Second recording: a 9:30 AM slot, and a 10 second lease.

12
00:00:52,567 --> 00:01:01,867
Ticket 41's agent cannot know if the visit is urgent, so it asks its person one question.

13
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:06,867
Nobody answers. The lease runs out, ticket 41 keeps its place, and the slot moves on.

14
00:01:06,867 --> 00:01:12,967
Ticket 42's agent asks too. Ana says no (recorded) and keeps her place.

15
00:01:12,967 --> 00:01:18,967
Sam wrote 'any time of day works'. His agent accepts without asking.

16
00:01:18,967 --> 00:01:22,100
Booked, and again the confirm sent twice made one booking.

17
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,600
Take a Number: a deli ticket, spoken between agents.
